Q3. What is the difference between if, if-else, and if-else-if statements? Explain each with a suitable example.


Answer:
if: Executes code when a condition is true.
if-else: Selects between two blocks of code.
if-else-if: Checks multiple conditions one by one.

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int marks = 80;

    if (marks >= 90) {
        cout << "Grade A+";
    }
    else if (marks >= 60) {
        cout << "Pass";
    }
    else {
        cout << "Fail";
    }

    return 0;
}
